  "description_short": "Premium Wagyu beef and harbour views at Mossel Bay's waterfront steakhouse.",
  "description_long": "Perched on Mossel Bay Harbour, The Marbled Wagyu brings quality steaks and ocean breezes together in a relaxed waterfront setting. The focus here is unashamedly on beef – specifically premium Wagyu cuts that arrive at your table perfectly prepared. While the steaks are the main attraction, the menu covers all the bases with fresh seafood, chicken options, and generous salads.\n\nThe location delivers what harbour restaurants should: working boats, gulls overhead, and that salty Garden Route air. Inside, it's modern and unfussy, but most visitors head straight for the outdoor tables where you can watch the comings and goings of the harbour between courses. The wine list leans local, with plenty of Western Cape reds to match the steaks. Staff know their cuts and cooking temperatures, making it easy for both steak novices and enthusiasts to order with confidence.\n\nIt's the kind of place that works for special occasions without feeling stuffy, or casual Friday nights when you're craving something more substantial than fish and chips. Booking ahead is wise, especially for sunset tables during summer months.",
